@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@
+BLOCKED: web.go request-ID chain order needs an owner fix (A-105 request-id clause)
+
+# T-102 — CSRF plumbing + middleware guards (M1)
+
+Everything this task owns is implemented, tested and green. The block is one
+clause of A-105 — the "request id" field of the served request log — because
+covering it requires reordering the middleware chain inside
+`internal/web/web.go`, which this task's `owns` forbid ("web.go is NOT in
+your owns — do not edit it. If you believe it needs a change, write BLOCKED
+instead"). This is that write.
+
+## The defect (pre-existing, from T-100's web.go)
+
+`Handler()` composes id-assigner-inner, logger-outer:
+
+- `web.go:62` `h = s.withRequestID(h)` (inner)
+- `web.go:63` `h = s.withLogging(h)` (outer)
+
+`withRequestID` enriches only its local request (`web.go:117`), so the outer
+`withLogging` still holds the pre-enrichment request when it logs
+(`web.go:141`), and `requestIDOf` (`context.go:28-33`) returns the `"-"`
+no-id sentinel. The response `X-Request-Id` header carries the real 16-hex
+id, so every served request line disagrees with its own header. The real
+binary does the same (`cmd/server/main.go:43` installs `srv.Handler()`
+unchanged), so prod logs every request with `req_id:"-"`. The protected
+acceptance test does not catch it: `acceptance/go/m1_guards_test.go:275-277`
+checks only that the `req_id` key is present and non-empty, which `"-"`
+satisfies.
+
+## Coverage statement (the point of this attempt)
+
+**No test in `internal/web` asserts the served chain's logged `req_id`.**
+Until web.go is fixed, A-105's request-id clause is unguarded below the
+acceptance suite, and nothing in this package claims otherwise:
+
+- `TestWithLoggingRequestFields` (runs the production `s.Handler()` chain)
+  asserts method, `pattern=` key presence + value, logged status
+  cross-checked against the actual `rec.Code` (and `rec.Code` against the
+  case's expected code), `dur_ms >= 0`, and that the response carries a real
+  16-hex `X-Request-Id` — the id-assigner half of the clause, which is
+  coverable and covered. It makes no assertion about the logged `req_id`;
+  the deliberate non-coverage is documented in a comment at the assertion
+  site.
+- `jsonRequestLine` / `TestProdLoggingIsJSON` check the JSON form of the
+  same coverable fields; the `req_id` check (previously key-presence /
+  non-empty, which the served `"-"` satisfies) is removed, with a comment
+  pointing here.
+- `TestWithLoggingLogsContextRequestID` (renamed from
+  `TestWithLoggingLogsRealRequestID`) is what it says: a **unit** test of
+  `withLogging`'s own contract — composed inside `withRequestID` (the
+  arrangement it was built for), the logged `req_id` equals the response
+  `X-Request-Id` and matches `^[0-9a-f]{16}$`, never `"-"`. Its doc comment
+  states explicitly that it is NOT production coverage and that whoever
+  swaps the two lines in web.go should move its assertion onto
+  `s.Handler()` so it guards the real chain.
+
+Why no failing assertion was left in place: the scheduler hard-fails on
+`make check-fast` before reviews run and the merge gate runs `make check`;
+a deliberately red test would keep this package — which T-103 compiles
+against — from ever merging. The review's sanctioned alternative ("removing/
+renaming the weak assertions so they are not represented as coverage") is
+what is implemented: the assertions that previously rubber-stamped `"-"` as
+acceptable are gone, not weakened further.
+
+## The owner fix (one line, web.go Handler() only)
+
+```go
+h = s.withLogging(h)      // swap with the line below
+h = s.withRequestID(h)
+```
+
+After the swap, move the assertion from `TestWithLoggingLogsContextRequestID`
+onto `s.Handler()` (logged `req_id` == response `X-Request-Id`, 16-hex,
+never `-`). Optionally also strengthen the protected
+`acceptance/go/m1_guards_test.go:275-277` from key-presence to the real-id
+shape — that file belongs to acceptance/'s owner, not this task.
+
+## What is delivered (committed on task/T-102)
+
+- `internal/web/csrf.go` — frozen double-submit API (unchanged this attempt;
+  both reviews found the implementation genuine). See "Frozen API" below.
+- `internal/web/csrf_test.go` — `TestCSRFTokenNameFrozen` (pins the
+  contract-frozen `csrf_token` literal), `TestCSRFVerify` (10-row table:
+  missing cookie, empty/spaces/short/non-base64url/padded/over-long/tampered
+  submissions, malformed cookie even when matched, valid round-trip — all
+  rejections uniformly `ErrCSRF`), `TestCSRFIssue` (now table-driven with
+  one row per flow: idempotent reuse with no redundant Set-Cookie, 32-byte
+  entropy floor, malformed-cookie reissue; the idempotency row now closes
+  the response body before counting cookies), `TestCSRFCookieFlags`
+  (prod/test table: Path=/, HttpOnly, SameSite=Lax, Secure iff prod).
+- `internal/web/middleware_logging_test.go` — the tests described under
+  "Coverage statement" above, plus `TestWithLoggingOmitsClientIP`
+  (RemoteAddr and injected X-Forwarded-For never appear) and
+  `TestMiddlewareGuards` (withRecover: panic→500+logged, clean
+  pass-through; withRequestID: header==context, ids differ per request).
+
+## Review-finding disposition (reviewer-alt, round 2)
+
+| Finding | Disposition |
+| --- | --- |
+| BLOCKING: served-chain req_id assertions pass on `-` | Removed entirely (value check, key-presence check and the `-v` t.Logf probe). Served-chain tests assert nothing about the logged req_id and say so in comments; the only request-id assertions that remain are the real 16-hex header check on the served chain and the unit-level real-id check in `TestWithLoggingLogsContextRequestID`. |
+| BLOCKING: composition test represented as the production guard | Renamed `TestWithLoggingLogsContextRequestID` and rescoped as a unit test of `withLogging`; its doc explicitly says NOT production coverage and hands the Handler()-level assertion to the web.go owner. The handoff no longer calls it "the real guard". |
+| 1: prod-JSON doc overstates "full field set" | Reworded to "every field coverable through the served chain", naming the exclusion. |
+| 2: TestCSRFIssue not table-driven | Converted to a table (`[]struct{name; run func(*testing.T)}`), one row per named case. |
+| 3: recorder Result() body not closed | Idempotency row closes the response body via defer before counting cookies. |
+| 4: t.Logf only visible under -v | The t.Logf is deleted along with the assertion it accompanied. |
+
+Round-1 findings (status cross-check vs `rec.Code`, `pattern=` key
+presence, frozen `csrf_token` literal, no scratch probes, no files outside
+owns) were addressed in the previous attempt and remain addressed.
+
+## Verification (this attempt, final tree)
+
+| Command | Exit | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `make e2e-task TASK=T-102` (baseline, pre-edit) | 0 | @A-102 4/4 projects; @A-105 has no Playwright spec (`--pass-with-no-tests`) — no red→green flip, as the packet states |
+| `make test-acceptance-go` (baseline) | 0 | `TestA105ProdLogsJSONNoIP`, `TestA101HealthzFast` green |
+| `make check-fast` | 0 | fmt-check, vet, golangci-lint "0 issues", `go test -race -count=1 -shuffle=on ./...` ok |
+| `go test ./internal/web/... -race -count=1` | 0 | ok 1.456s |
+| `make cover` | 0 | internal/web 86.7%, internal/config 81.1% (floor 70) |
+| `make e2e-task TASK=T-102` (final) | 0 | 4 passed (desktop-chromium, pixel-9, iphone-16, iphone-se-320) |
+| `make test-acceptance-go` (final) | 0 | acceptance/go ok |
+| `git status --porcelain` | 0 | only this task's two test files modified; no `test-run.db`/`test-run-photos/` created; sole untracked entry is the pre-existing `node_modules` (guard-allowlisted, not committed) |
+
+## Frozen API as implemented (T-103 compiles against this — unchanged)
+
+```go
+// internal/web/csrf.go — package web
+const CSRFTokenName = "csrf_token" // cookie name AND hidden-input name (contract-frozen string)
+
+var ErrCSRF = errors.New("csrf: token mismatch")
+
+func IssueCSRFToken(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) string
+func VerifyCSRF(r *http.Request, submitted string) error
+```
+
+Semantics T-103 should rely on:
+
+- **Token format**: 32 crypto/rand bytes as unpadded base64url (43 chars).
+  "Well-formed" = strict raw-url decode to >= 32 bytes, length <= 256 (DoS
+  bound on hostile cookies/fields).
+- **IssueCSRFToken**: a well-formed `csrf_token` request cookie is reused
+  as-is with **no Set-Cookie** (idempotent per session-less phase; pinned).
+  Otherwise a fresh token is minted and set: `Path=/`, `HttpOnly`,
+  `SameSite=Lax`, `Secure` iff `serverFrom(r.Context()).Cfg.IsProd()`. Must
+  run inside the server chain (needs the server in context, like every
+  handler). On the unreachable entropy failure it answers 500 and returns "".
+- **VerifyCSRF**: nil only if cookie and submission both exist, are
+  well-formed, and are equal under crypto/subtle constant-time compare.
+  Everything else — missing cookie, empty, garbage, short, padded,
+  over-long, mismatched — is `ErrCSRF`, uniformly (answer 403, don't
+  distinguish causes).
+- **Usage sketch for /probe**: render: `tok := IssueCSRFToken(w, r)` then
+  `<input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{.CSRFToken}}">`; POST:
+  parse the form into a typed struct at the boundary, then
+  `if err := VerifyCSRF(r, f.CSRFToken); err != nil { 403 }`.
+
+## Open issues
+
+1. The blocked item itself (see top): one-line `web.go` chain-order fix by
+   whoever owns `web.go`; moving the real-id assertion onto `s.Handler()`;
+   optional matching strengthening of the protected A-105 acceptance
+   assertion by whoever owns `acceptance/`.
+2. Until then, A-105's request-id clause is enforced only as far as the
+   protected acceptance suite enforces it (key presence), and this package's
+   unit suite deliberately makes no claim on it.
+3. Untracked `node_modules` (Playwright install) predates this attempt, is
+   allowlisted by the guard, and is not committed.
